{"name":"Chicken Comb","hex":"#dd2222","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chicken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated subspecies of red junglefowl (Gallus gallus domesticus).","The meat from this bird eaten as food."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cowardly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken"},{"term":"comb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A toothed implement:\nA toothed implement for grooming the hair or (formerly) for keeping it in place.\n\nA machine used in separating choice cotton fibers from worsted cloth fibers.\nThe toothed plate at the top and bottom of an escalator that prevents objects getting trapped between the moving stairs and fixed landings.\nA toothed tool used for chasing screws on work in a lathe; a chaser.\nThe notched scale of a wire micrometer.\nThe collector of an electrical machine, usually resembling a comb.\nA toothed plate used for creating wells in agar gels for electrophoresis.\n A toothed wooden pick used to push the weft thread tightly against the previous pass of thread to create a tight weave.\nOne of a pair of peculiar organs on the base of the abdomen in scorpions, with which they comb substrate.\nA ctene.","A toothed implement for grooming the hair or (formerly) for keeping it in place."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Especially of hair or fur, to groom with a toothed implement, especially a comb.","To separate choice cotton fibers from worsted cloth fibers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"},{"title":"Comb","blocks":[{"text":"A comb is a tool consisting of a shaft that holds a row of teeth for pulling through the hair to clean, untangle, or style it. Combs have been used since prehistoric times, having been discovered in very refined forms from settlements dating back to 5,000 years ago in Persia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Plastic_comb%2C_2015-06-07.jpg/330px-Plastic_comb%2C_2015-06-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comb","wikidata":"Q23834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGLW_2_global_distributions_of_c)_chickens.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Rooster_portrait2.jpg/500px-Rooster_portrait2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Rooster_portrait2.jpg/1280px-Rooster_portrait2.jpg?utm_sourc